# Temporary OpenCode2 / Aether compatibility workaround (2026-10-02).
# Aether drops functionResponse.id while retaining functionCall.id; use V1-style
# ID-less tool history while the gateway remains pinned to Aether 0.7.13.
#
# Removal gate: upgrade to an Aether release fixing BOTH issues:
# - Responses SSE corruption: https://github.com/fawney19/Aether/issues/814
# - Asymmetric Gemini ID stripping: https://github.com/fawney19/Aether/issues/878
# Upgrading alone is insufficient: v0.7.19 still strips functionResponse.id.
# Verify large Responses SSE events remain intact, then verify unpatched OpenCode2
# single, sequential and same-name parallel Gemini tool calls through that gateway
# retain matching call/response IDs and correctly paired results.
# Then remove this file, its launcher.nix entry, and the
# google.options.omitFunctionCallIds override in default.nix.

